  "term": "magnitude estimation",
  "definition": "Magnitude estimation is the process of judging or producing the size of a quantity, such as how many items are present or where a number belongs on a number line. In this source, it refers specifically to estimating number magnitude in tasks involving non-symbolic quantities and number line judgments.",
